## Overview

Amazon EFS (Elastic File System) is a fully managed, serverless, set-and-forget elastic file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It provides a simple, scalable, and highly available shared file storage that can be mounted on multiple EC2 instances simultaneously.

**Key Difference from EBS:**
- **EBS**: Block storage, attached to single EC2 instance
- **EFS**: Network file system, shared across multiple EC2 instances in same VPC

**Key Characteristics:**
- Shared file system accessible from multiple EC2 instances
- Automatic scaling (grows and shrinks automatically)
- Highly available and durable
- Pay only for what you use (no pre-provisioning)
- Supports both Linux and containerized applications

