## Key Concepts

### 1. File System
- Distributed storage for sharing files across multiple EC2 instances
- Mounted via NFS (Network File System) v4.1 protocol
- Accessible from EC2 instances in same VPC and optionally on-premises

### 2. Mount Targets
- Network interface in a subnet through which instances mount EFS
- Must create mount target in each AZ you want to access EFS
- Each mount target has IP address in the subnet

### 3. Security Groups
- Control traffic between EC2 instances and mount targets
- Require NFS protocol (port 2049) inbound access

### 4. Automatic Scaling
- No provisioning required
- File system grows and shrinks automatically
- No performance degradation as storage grows

### 5. Replication and Durability
- Data replicated across multiple AZs (standard)
- One Zone storage class for single-AZ deployment

### 6. Access Points
- Enforce a user identity and root directory for applications
- Simplify access control and application-level permissions
- Enforce directory-level permissions

