## Storage Classes

### 1. Standard Storage Class
- Default, recommended for most workloads
- Full support for all EFS features
- Data in all AZs simultaneously

```bash
# Create with Standard storage (default)
aws efs create-file-system \
  --availability-zone-name us-east-1a \
  --encrypted \
  --tags Key=Name,Value=StandardEFS
```

### 2. One Zone Storage Class
- Single-AZ storage
- 50% cheaper than Standard
- Data replicated within single AZ only
- Suitable for non-critical, non-production workloads

```bash
# Create with One Zone storage
aws efs create-file-system \
  --storage-redundancy-type ONE_ZONE \
  --encrypted \
  --tags Key=Name,Value=OneZoneEFS
```

### 3. Infrequent Access (IA) Storage Class
- Automatically transitions files to lower-cost IA storage
- Reactivated when accessed
- Cost: ~95% cheaper than Standard for infrequent access patterns

```bash
# Create with IA lifecycle
aws efs put-lifecycle-configuration \
  --file-system-id fs-12345678 \
  --lifecycle-policies TransitionToIA=AFTER_30_DAYS
```

