### Example 3: Enable Lifecycle Policies (Infrequent Access)

```bash
# Enable automatic transition to Infrequent Access
aws efs put-lifecycle-configuration \
  --file-system-id fs-1234567890abcdef0 \
  --lifecycle-policies TransitionToIA=AFTER_30_DAYS,TransitionToPrimaryStorageClass=AFTER_1_HOUR

# Verify lifecycle configuration
aws efs describe-lifecycle-configuration \
  --file-system-id fs-1234567890abcdef0
```

**Output:**
```json
{
  "LifecyclePolicies": [
    {
      "TransitionToIA": "AFTER_30_DAYS"
    },
    {
      "TransitionToPrimaryStorageClass": "AFTER_1_HOUR"
    }
  ]
}
```

**How It Works:**
1. Files not accessed for 30 days automatically move to IA storage
2. When file is accessed, it transitions back to standard storage
3. Cost: 95% cheaper for IA storage, minimal access penalty

