### Example 4: Monitor EFS Performance with CloudWatch

```bash
# Get file system metrics
aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
  --namespace AWS/EFS \
  --metric-name BurstCreditBalance \
  --dimensions Name=FileSystemId,Value=fs-1234567890abcdef0 \
  --start-time 2025-11-25T00:00:00Z \
  --end-time 2025-11-25T23:59:59Z \
  --period 3600 \
  --statistics Average,Minimum

# Get throughput metrics
aws cloudwatch get-metric-statistics \
  --namespace AWS/EFS \
  --metric-name TotalIOBytes \
  --dimensions Name=FileSystemId,Value=fs-1234567890abcdef0 \
  --start-time 2025-11-25T00:00:00Z \
  --end-time 2025-11-25T23:59:59Z \
  --period 300 \
  --statistics Sum
```

**Key Metrics to Monitor:**
- **BurstCreditBalance:** Available burst capacity (bursting mode)
- **PermittedThroughput:** Max allowed throughput
- **ClientConnections:** Number of EC2 instances connected
- **TotalIOBytes:** Total bytes read/written
- **MeteredIOBytes:** Metered operations (billed operations)

